# The llama.cpp pins, one b-build per host class, and the repository of ggml's images. A class's
# build serves each of its flavors: host/llama.sh names the server image server-<flavor>-<build> in
# LLAMA_REPOSITORY, and llama_pin (host/llama-release.sh) reads the class's pin. strix-halo (the
# Framework; rocm and vulkan) runs the b-build named ("Nightly build:") in the notes of the semver
# release LLAMA_RELEASE. gb10 (gb10-1; cuda13) runs b12098, the 2026-11-04 nightly image, which
# spike-hosting-upgrades' screen adopted (docs/screens/gb10-1/2026-11-05.md; the engine rule rolled
# it back and the architect overruled it). It is held below newer builds: llama.cpp #31620 and
# #31639 (b12100 and later) match an -hf quantization tag only after `-`, `.` or `/`, and Google's
# QAT GGUFs (such as gemma-4-26B_q4_0-it.gguf) put `_` before it, so no Google QAT section resolves
# on them; revisit when Google renames its QAT GGUFs or llama.cpp accepts `_`. strix-halo (the
# Framework) is held on b11960 until its next session's host update: its re-screen of Gemma 4
# 26B-A4B waits on llama.cpp #25584, the fix for #29221 (Vulkan's "tensor not allocated" abort on
# a 15-slot section's second request), and #31418 (Vulkan's batched tensor copy API), so
# currency reports it behind (spike-hosting-upgrades, docs/screens/framework/2026-11-04.md and
# docs/screens/gb10-1/2026-11-05.md). scripts/currency.sh
# compares each class's pin with the newest b-build that has the class's server image on ghcr.io,
# not with LLAMA_RELEASE's build. Sourced by host/llama-release.sh.
LLAMA_RELEASE=v0.8.0
LLAMA_BUILD_GB10=b12098
LLAMA_BUILD_STRIX_HALO=b11960
LLAMA_REPOSITORY=ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp
